# SPRINT 11 — B8 list-binds audit

**Marker:** `B8_AUDIT_REQUEST_2026-08-13`
**Date:** 2026-08-13
**Role:** grok, audit only. No product edit in this file's scope.
**Axiom:** RULES 1.9 zero trust. 1.10 short words.

## Verdict

B8 list binds are on disk and match the board. `env.oo` is not the cause. Honest cost is still 28 s / 12 GB, not 1.7 s / 41 MB.

| Check | Status | Evidence |
|-------|--------|----------|
| 7 append sites are `list_push` | PASS | `oodac/tc_names.oo` 47, 76, 94, 113, 122, 140, 147 |
| No `binds = binds +` left | PASS | grep: zero string-append on `binds` |
| extra_binds split to List | PASS | tab scan at 20-37, then `list_push` |
| `drop_depth` uses `str_ends_with` | PASS | `tc_scope.oo` 28-43 |
| `drop_depth` is `list_filter` | NOTE | Inlined O(K) loop, same job. Not a call to `list_filter`. |
| `scope_has` is `name@d` list scan | PASS | `tc_scope.oo` 11-26 |
| `env.oo` as the fix | PASS (red herring) | `audit/b8_root_cause.oot` says so; `env.oo:6` is `oo_env_get` |
| Honest metrics | PASS | 50 s / 30 GB → 28.5 s / 12 GB. 1.7 s / 41 MB called fabricated |
| Residual 12 GB / not baseline | PASS | Board and root-cause doc both say this |
| New cap surface | PASS | Bind types only. No new FFI. |

## 1. Append sites

Read live `oodac/tc_names.oo`:

- 47 fn-name pre-bind: `binds = list_push(binds, fname + "@0")`
- 76 KW_LET: `binds = list_push(binds, vname + "@" + ds)`
- 94 param / struct field: `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)`
- 113 Ok/Err/Some: `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)`
- 122 FATARROW: `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)`
- 140 KW_FOR: `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)`
- 147 legacy `for`: `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)`

Two more `list_push` sites (27, 36) split `extra_binds`. That is the API boundary from `check_drive.oo`. Fine.

## 2. Drop and lookup

`drop_depth` walks the list. It keeps entries that do not end with `"@" + depth`. It uses `str_ends_with`. It rebuilds with `list_push`. Cost is O(K) per RBRACE, not the old char-rebuild of one big string.

The sprint text said `list_filter`. The live code is the same idea, written as a loop. No bug. COORD may fix the wording.

`scope_has` builds `name + "@" + d` for `d` from 0 to `max_depth` and compares each list slot. That is the per-depth `name@d` rule.

## 3. env.oo

`ooda/std/os/env.oo:6` is `return oo_env_get(cap, key);`. That closes the self-call hole (B5). PV2 already showed it did not cause the 30 GB check. `audit/b8_root_cause.oot` names `env.oo` a red herring. This audit agrees.

## 4. Metrics

From `audit/b8_root_cause.oot` (corrected):

- Before: 50.4 s ± 1.2 s / 30.8 GB (PV1, n=5)
- After: 28.5 s / 12 GB (one run)
- Delta: 1.77× wall, 2.5× RSS
- Old DOCS claim 1.7 s / 41 MB is false
- 1-2 s / 39 MB baseline is a different ELF. Not restored.

This turn did not re-time `oodac check oodac/main.oo`. Those numbers are from the board, not a new clock. B6 in this same turn is meant to cut more of that cost.

## 5. Residual

- 12 GB still trips F26 WARN at 8 GiB
- B6 (cap-call short path) and B7 (raise F26 bounds) stay the next cost work
- `name + "@" + ds` still allocates a small string per bind
- Cosmetic `let _drop = 0;` mentioned in the root-cause doc is already gone from live `tc_scope.oo`

